{"parentUuid":"c29c98cb-ebd3-4a02-85a0-3b25e7131a73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01PhWY65YuExVBMaEFTMAAuv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both mysteries are solved. Here's what I found.\n\n## 1. The Documents-tab error — known bug, fix exists but never shipped\n\nThe Documents tab's graph widget falls back to reading the raw `/graph/full` dump when `/kg3d/ontology` returns empty. In v1.10.0 that fallback computes `Math.max(1, ...degree.values())` — spreading one function argument per node. Your longview workspace is now at ~30k concepts after synthesis, and spreading tens of thousands of arguments overflows the JS call stack. That's your exact error.\n\nThe fix (incremental max + a 400-node render budget, in [index.js:331](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/kg3d/synoptic_web/index.js:331)) is sitting **uncommitted in your working tree** — it was written after v1.10.0 was tagged, so the installer you just put on has the broken version. It needs a commit and a v1.10.1 patch release to reach the installed app.\n\n## 2. Why there's no AI Vampire book — a cascade, ending in a fatal crash\n\nThe ledger tells the whole overnight story (Jul 2→3, UTC):\n\n1. **model phase** — the deep-synthesis ingest of 32 card docs hit its 4-hour timeout at 01:04. At 30k concepts the runtime's full clustering pass after the batch is enormous, and because the client gave up, those files were never marked ingested (they'll be re-attempted every run).\n2. **code phase** failed (the cp1252/braille-spinner Unicode crash — the `PYTHONIOENCODING` fix didn't take; still broken).\n3. **weave phase** got zero parseable discovery questions and stopped — the discovery directory is empty.\n4. **reduce phase** ran while lemonade was still recovering from the synthesis grind: the **prime-silo dossier came back with 0 completion tokens and is a 0-byte file**. Your flagship project is absent from THEMES, the report, the PRD, and everything downstream. (Also: \"benny\" and \"Benny\" dossiers collide on Windows' case-insensitive filesystem — the good one happened to win.)\n5. **reduce book** — the outline JSON was truncated at the output budget (the file literally ends mid-object, no closing brace), so chapters were skipped. The `book/BOOK.md` you have is the stale Jul-2 one.\n6. **opus phase — the actual killer.** The outline call returned JSON that passed `jsonCall`'s weak check (`parts != null`) but failed the strict `parts.length` check in [opus.mjs:112](prime-silo/scripts/longview/lib/opus.mjs:112), which **throws**. `runManifest` has no per-phase try/catch, so the throw killed the entire process — no outline written, zero sections, and the **pdf phase never ran**. A second run started minutes later, re-mapped some cards, and died silently mid-ingest around 02:10 (last ledger entry). Right now nothing is running: no lock, the runtime's task queue is empty, and lemonade is healthy.\n\n## Should you decouple the book? Yes — and it's 90% decoupled already\n\nThe good news: the opus phase **doesn't need ingestion at all**. It reads THEMES.md + dossiers from disk and pulls evidence via retrieval from vectors/graph that already exist. `benny longview run --phase opus` (or `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs opus`) is already a standalone, resume-safe-per-section entry point. What actually needs fixing is small:\n\n1. **Phase isolation** — wrap each phase in `runManifest` in try/catch so a phase failure is ledgered and the run continues (this alone would have given you a book attempt + PDF last night).\n2. **Opus outline validation** — make `jsonCall` require a *non-empty array*, so the built-in retry actually fires instead of the strict check throwing fatally afterward.\n3. **Run order/scheduling** — never let the multi-hour deep-synthesis ingest share the box with the LLM reduce/opus phases; it wedges lemonade and produces those 0-token outputs. Ingest should be its own scheduled run (or vectors-only for cards at this graph size, like you already decided for weave notes).\n4. **Before regenerating the book**: rerun dossiers (`--phase reduce` with `only: [\"dossiers\",\"themes\"]`) so prime-silo isn't a 0-byte hole in the book's foundation. ~25 minutes at the observed ~90s/dossier.\n\nSo the sequence I'd recommend: apply fixes 1–2, regenerate dossiers + themes, then run `opus` → `pdf` standalone. Total book run is roughly 100 sections × ~1–2 min on qwen3.5-9b — a few hours, but resume-safe and independent of any ingest.\n\nWant me to apply the two code fixes and kick off the dossier-repair → opus → pdf sequence? I can also commit the kg3d stack-overflow fix alongside so v1.10.1 is ready to cut."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2913,"cache_read_input_tokens":120456,"output_tokens":2369,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2913,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2369,"cache_read_input_tokens":120456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2913},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcegQHRW47RcEANtgNUDk","type":"assistant","uuid":"ab999782-d49e-4b59-b696-7013a47f5e7a","timestamp":"2026-07-03T06:51:23.113Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"7aba7344-6e98-4c00-b7e9-ad132cfe087b","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
