{"parentUuid":"2d4935e9-e1e1-4cd5-940c-b59b50b34655","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"717b417c-07ea-42e4-81cf-55fba4dccdfa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015K3WpnzDuyRvH7pew2pXMd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# LONGVIEW — run & test guide\n2\t\n3\tTurns months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\n4\tmemo-ray entity store) into a workspace knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\n5\tportfolio report, PRD, operator skill, project dossiers, book, TOGAF prep — all\n6\ton the local model, for electricity instead of tokens.\n7\t\n8\t- Design: [`architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`](../../architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md)\n9\t- Definition of record: [`manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json`](../../manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json)\n10\t- Runner internals: [`scripts/longview/README.md`](../../../scripts/longview/README.md)\n11\t\n12\t## Prerequisites\n13\t\n14\t| What | Check |\n15\t| ---- | ----- |\n16\t| Lemonade on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` | `curl http://127.0.0.1:13305/api/v1/models` |\n17\t| Benny runtime on `:8005` | `curl -H \"X-Benny-API-Key: benny-mesh-2026-auth\" http://127.0.0.1:8005/api/offload/health` |\n18\t| memo-ray checkout sibling of prime-silo | its server running is optional (sync falls back to direct parsers) |\n19\t| Node.js on PATH | the runner is Node; `benny longview` shells out to it |\n20\t\n21\tThe workspace lives under the **runtime's resolved home** (desktop config →\n22\te.g. `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny\\workspaces\\longview`), never the\n23\trepo. The runner resolves it identically via `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`.\n24\t\n25\t## Run from the EXE (v1.9.1+)\n26\t\n27\tNo terminal needed — both surfaces call the same launcher and read the same\n28\tdisk-truth status (runner lock + heartbeat), so runs started anywhere show\n29\teverywhere:\n30\t\n31\t- **Tray** — right-click Prime-Silo: `LONGVIEW: idle/running (…)` status line,\n32\t  **Run LONGVIEW delta sync**, **Stop LONGVIEW (resume-safe)**, and\n33\t  **Open LONGVIEW outputs**.\n34\t- **Bridge → Documents** (workspace `longview`) — the **LONGVIEW pipeline**\n35\t  panel: *Run delta sync* / *Run full pipeline* / *Stop*, with a live heartbeat\n36\t  (phase, cards done/total, failures, ETA) and the last runner log line while\n37\t  running. Deliverables appear below in **Outputs**.\n38\t- **API** — `POST /api/longview_run {\"mode\":\"delta\"|\"all\"|\"<phase>\"}`,\n39\t  `GET /api/longview_status`, `POST /api/longview_stop`.\n40\t\n41\tThe child process logs to `<workspace>/longview/runner.log`; only one runner\n42\tper workspace can hold the lock, regardless of launcher.\n43\t\n44\t## Commands (all from `prime-silo/runtime/`)\n45\t\n46\t```powershell\n47\tpython benny_cli.py longview run                  # all enabled phases, resume-safe\n48\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --phase map      # one phase (also retries failed cards)\n49\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --delta          # only new/changed sessions\n50\tpython benny_cli.py longview status               # heartbeat: phase, counts, ETA\n51\tpython benny_cli.py longview report               # honest ledger report\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tPhases (declared in the manifest, executed in order):\n55\t`inventory` → `extract` → `map` → `model` → `code` → `weave` → `reduce` → `opus` → `pdf`.\n56\tEdit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, `deep_synthesis`,\n57\tloop counts, or to disable phases — no code changes.\n58\t\n59\t- **code** — junctions the repo into `<workspace>/src/` and runs `benny enrich`\n60\t  (Tree-Sitter scan → code graph → `CORRELATES_WITH` links to the knowledge\n61\t  concepts). The dual graph is what lets later phases cross-reference decisions\n62\t  to the code they shaped.\n63\t- **weave** — discovery loops (`weave_loops` × `weave_questions`): the model\n64\t  proposes under-explored questions, each is answered from retrieval (vector\n65\t  chunks + graph concepts) into a **cited discovery note**, and the notes are\n66\t  ingested back — so every loop, and every deliverable after it, stands on a\n67\t  richer corpus. This is the compounding \"greater than the sum\" mechanism.\n68\t- **opus** — *The AI Vampire*: a 200+ page narrative-nonfiction book built\n69\t  hierarchically (one outline call → per-chapter section specs → ~100\n70\t  retrieval-grounded sections of 650–950 words, each cited, each resume-safe\n71\t  as a file under `data_out/opus/sections/`). Assembles to\n72\t  `data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.md`; partial assemblies are valid previews.\n73\t- **pdf** — the assembled book → print-styled HTML → PDF via headless\n74\t  Edge/Chrome: `data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.pdf`.\n75\t\n76\t## Test procedure (small slice first, then the whole)\n77\t\n78\t1. **Pilot the map** — prove the local model produces gated cards:\n79\t   ```powershell\n80\t   node ../scripts/longview/longview.mjs inventory\n81\t   node ../scripts/longview/longview.mjs extract\n82\t   node ../scripts/longview/longview.mjs map --limit 5\n83\t   python benny_cli.py longview report     # expect cards ok > 0, failures listed by sid\n84\t   ```\n85\t2. **Prove resume** — Ctrl+C mid-map, rerun the same command: the queue must\n86\t   shrink by exactly the already-ledgered sessions.\n87\t3. **Prove the graph** — run the model phase, then check Neo4j actually filled\n88\t   (Chroma chunks alone are NOT the graph):\n89\t   ```powershell\n90\t   python benny_cli.py longview run --phase model\n91\t   # then: MCP get_graph_stats(workspace=\"longview\"), or Bridge → Documents →\n92\t   # knowledge graph. Expect Concept nodes + RELATES_TO / SOURCED_FROM edges.\n93\t   ```\n94\t4. **Full run** — `python benny_cli.py longview run` and walk away. Reference\n95\t   throughput on this box: ~52 cards/hour (map), LLM-per-document synthesis in\n96\t   the model phase (~2–5 min/doc), reduce ≈ 30–60 min.\n97\t5. **Deliverables**