{"parentUuid":"0cd3acf4-f0f5-4df1-9653-9872366abb58","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"717b417c-07ea-42e4-81cf-55fba4dccdfa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011YuNptVvRGkuZZDDcpRvjT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# LONGVIEW — long-horizon session synthesis (ADR-005)\n2\t\n3\tTurns 9 months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\n4\tmemo-ray entity store) into a queryable knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\n5\ta portfolio report, a PRD for what comes next, an operator skill, a book, and a\n6\tTOGAF SAD — all generated by the local model (Lemonade `qwen3.5-9b-FLM`), for\n7\telectricity instead of tokens.\n8\t\n9\tDesign: `runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`.\n10\t\n11\t## Prerequisites\n12\t\n13\t- Lemonade serving on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (or set `LONGVIEW_MODEL`).\n14\t  The FLM recipe currently loads with `ctx_size 4096`, which caps evidence packs\n15\t  at 7500 chars and reduce inputs at 8500 chars (both enforced). **Raising the\n16\t  FLM ctx_size to 16384+** and setting `LONGVIEW_EVIDENCE_BUDGET=12000` /\n17\t  `LONGVIEW_REDUCE_INPUT=30000` buys noticeably higher-fidelity synthesis.\n18\t- Benny runtime on `:8005` (only needed for Phase D graph ingestion + TOGAF run).\n19\t  The workspace lives under the **runtime's resolved home** (desktop config →\n20\t  `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny` on this box) — `lib/config.mjs`\n21\t  resolves it with `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`, same as the runtime.\n22\t- memo-ray checkout as a sibling of prime-silo (or set `MEMORAY_DATA_DIR`);\n23\t  its server running is optional — sync falls back to invoking the parsers.\n24\t\n25\t## Manifest mode (the managed way — use this)\n26\t\n27\tThe pipeline definition of record is\n28\t`runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` (variables + phases).\n29\tRun and manage it from the Benny CLI:\n30\t\n31\t```powershell\n32\tcd prime-silo/runtime\n33\tpython benny_cli.py longview run                  # all enabled phases, resume-safe\n34\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --phase model    # one phase\n35\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --delta          # only new/changed sessions\n36\tpython benny_cli.py longview status               # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)\n37\tpython benny_cli.py longview report               # honest ledger report\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t(Equivalent direct form: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs run [manifest] [--phase X] [--delta]`.)\n41\tPer ADR-005 §4 the manifest's tasks are the five _phases_ — the per-session\n42\tfan-out stays inside the map phase's checkpointed loop, never as swarm tasks.\n43\tEdit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, or to disable phases.\n44\t\n45\tResume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it\n46\tcontinues where the ledger says it stopped. Delta reduce re-runs automatically\n47\tonce ≥5 new cards accumulate (`delta_reduce_threshold`).\n48\t\n49\t## Graph ingestion (deep synthesis)\n50\t\n51\t`deep_synthesis: true` in the manifest is what turns card docs into\n52\tDocument/Concept nodes in Neo4j — without it `/rag/ingest` writes **vectors\n53\tonly** and the knowledge-graph views stay empty (found live: 55 cards in\n54\tChroma, zero graph nodes). Synthesis is LLM-per-document, so ingest batches\n55\tare small (`ingest_batch_size: 5`) and slow; the phase is idempotent (old\n56\tvectors per source are deleted before re-add), so re-running `--phase model`\n57\tafter clearing `longview/rollups/ingested.json` back-fills the graph.\n58\t\n59\t## Phases (runnable individually)\n60\t\n61\t| Phase     | Command     | What                                                       | LLM? |\n62\t| --------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ---- |\n63\t| inventory | `inventory` | memo-ray sync + session census                             | no   |\n64\t| extract   | `extract`   | deterministic evidence packs (≤9 KB each)                  | no   |\n65\t| map       | `map`       | evidence → session cards, gated + ledgered (the long part) | yes  |\n66\t| model     | `model`     | rollups + cards into the workspace knowledge graph         | no\\* |\n67\t| reduce    | `reduce`    | dossiers → themes → report/PRD/skill/book (+ TOGAF prep)   | yes  |\n68\t\n69\t\\* `model` calls Benny `/rag/ingest`, which embeds locally. Skip with `--no-graph`.\n70\t\n71\t## Where things land\n72\t\n73\t```\n74\t$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/longview/\n75\t├── longview/            state: inventory, evidence/, cards/, rollups/,\n76\t│                        ledger.jsonl (honesty), status.json (heartbeat)\n77\t├── data_in/             session-card markdown (graph corpus)\n78\t└── data_out/            deliverables:\n79\t    ├── PORTFOLIO-REPORT.md, THEMES.md, PRD-WHAT-COMES-NEXT.md\n80\t    ├── dossiers/<project>.md, skills/working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md\n81\t    ├── book/BOOK.md (+ outline.json, chapter-NN.md)\n82\t    └── TOGAF-RUN.md     the human-launched SAD swarm command (ADR-001)\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tDeliverables are proposals in `data_out/` — promoting a skill into\n86\t`~/.claude/skills`, or the PRD into the roadmap, stays a human step.\n87\t\n88\t## Observability\n89\t\n90\t- `status.json` — updated after every card; Bridge's file browser can watch it.\n91\t- `ledger.jsonl` — append-only; `report` reads only this. Numbers not in the\n92\t  ledger don't get claimed (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n93\t- Phase D ingestion and the TOGAF swarm run in the Benny runtime ⇒ visible in\n94\t  Mission Control / the activity feed like any other run.\n95\t- Lemonade's own console shows live generation.\n96\t\n97\t## Honest limitations (v1)\n98\t\n99\t- 63 of 130 indexed sessions are \"thin\" (empty brain dirs; conversations exist\n100\t  only as unparsed protobuf). They are ledgered `skipped_thin`, not guessed at.\n101\t  A `.pb` decoder or the `antigravity-backup/` dirs would raise coverage.\n102\t- Claude coverage in the memo-ray store is 7 sessions vs 36 transcript files on\n103\t  disk — worth a look at `claudeParser` thresholds.\n104\t- Card quality has a 9B ceiling; every claim carries session-id citations so\n105\t  weak cards are visible and re-runnable (`map --force` after deleting a card).\n106\t"}]},"uuid":"a3d4f5b6-d6b3-4687-b4f8-c75cfe29e0f3","timestamp":"2026-07-03T07:03:10.096Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\README.md","content":"# LONGVIEW — long-horizon session synthesis (ADR-005)\n\nTurns 9 months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\nmemo-ray entity store) into a queryable knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\na portfolio report, a PRD for what comes next, an operator skill, a book, and a\nTOGAF SAD — all generated by the local model (Lemonade `qwen3.5-9b-FLM`), for\nelectricity instead of tokens.\n\nDesign: `runtime/architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Lemonade serving on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (or set `LONGVIEW_MODEL`).\n  The FLM recipe currently loads with `ctx_size 4096`, which caps evidence packs\n  at 7500 chars and reduce inputs at 8500 chars (both enforced). **Raising the\n  FLM ctx_size to 16384+** and setting `LONGVIEW_EVIDENCE_BUDGET=12000` /\n  `LONGVIEW_REDUCE_INPUT=30000` buys noticeably higher-fidelity synthesis.\n- Benny runtime on `:8005` (only needed for Phase D graph ingestion + TOGAF run).\n  The workspace lives under the **runtime's resolved home** (desktop config →\n  `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny` on this box) — `lib/config.mjs`\n  resolves it with `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`, same as the runtime.\n- memo-ray checkout as a sibling of prime-silo (or set `MEMORAY_DATA_DIR`);\n  its server running is optional — sync falls back to invoking the parsers.\n\n## Manifest mode (the managed way — use this)\n\nThe pipeline definition of record is\n`runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` (variables + phases).\nRun and manage it from the Benny CLI:\n\n```powershell\ncd prime-silo/runtime\npython benny_cli.py longview run                  # all enabled phases, resume-safe\npython benny_cli.py longview run --phase model    # one phase\npython benny_cli.py longview run --delta          # only new/changed sessions\npython benny_cli.py longview status               # live heartbeat (phase, ETA, rates)\npython benny_cli.py longview report               # honest ledger report\n```\n\n(Equivalent direct form: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs run [manifest] [--phase X] [--delta]`.)\nPer ADR-005 §4 the manifest's tasks are the five _phases_ — the per-session\nfan-out stays inside the map phase's checkpointed loop, never as swarm tasks.\nEdit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, or to disable phases.\n\nResume-safe at card granularity: Ctrl+C anytime, rerun the same command, it\ncontinues where the ledger says it stopped. Delta reduce re-runs automatically\nonce ≥5 new cards accumulate (`delta_reduce_threshold`).\n\n## Graph ingestion (deep synthesis)\n\n`deep_synthesis: true` in the manifest is what turns card docs into\nDocument/Concept nodes in Neo4j — without it `/rag/ingest` writes **vectors\nonly** and the knowledge-graph views stay empty (found live: 55 cards in\nChroma, zero graph nodes). Synthesis is LLM-per-document, so ingest batches\nare small (`ingest_batch_size: 5`) and slow; the phase is idempotent (old\nvectors per source are deleted before re-add), so re-running `--phase model`\nafter clearing `longview/rollups/ingested.json` back-fills the graph.\n\n## Phases (runnable individually)\n\n| Phase     | Command     | What                                                       | LLM? |\n| --------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ---- |\n| inventory | `inventory` | memo-ray sync + session census                             | no   |\n| extract   | `extract`   | deterministic evidence packs (≤9 KB each)                  | no   |\n| map       | `map`       | evidence → session cards, gated + ledgered (the long part) | yes  |\n| model     | `model`     | rollups + cards into the workspace knowledge graph         | no\\* |\n| reduce    | `reduce`    | dossiers → themes → report/PRD/skill/book (+ TOGAF prep)   | yes  |\n\n\\* `model` calls Benny `/rag/ingest`, which embeds locally. Skip with `--no-graph`.\n\n## Where things land\n\n```\n$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/longview/\n├── longview/            state: inventory, evidence/, cards/, rollups/,\n│                        ledger.jsonl (honesty), status.json (heartbeat)\n├── data_in/             session-card markdown (graph corpus)\n└── data_out/            deliverables:\n    ├── PORTFOLIO-REPORT.md, THEMES.md, PRD-WHAT-COMES-NEXT.md\n    ├── dossiers/<project>.md, skills/working-with-this-operator.SKILL.md\n    ├── book/BOOK.md (+ outline.json, chapter-NN.md)\n    └── TOGAF-RUN.md     the human-launched SAD swarm command (ADR-001)\n```\n\nDeliverables are proposals in `data_out/` — promoting a skill into\n`~/.claude/skills`, or the PRD into the roadmap, stays a human step.\n\n## Observability\n\n- `status.json` — updated after every card; Bridge's file browser can watch it.\n- `ledger.jsonl` — append-only; `report` reads only this. Numbers not in the\n  ledger don't get claimed (memo-ray token-audit lesson).\n- Phase D ingestion and the TOGAF swarm run in the Benny runtime ⇒ visible in\n  Mission Control / the activity feed like any other run.\n- Lemonade's own console shows live generation.\n\n## Honest limitations (v1)\n\n- 63 of 130 indexed sessions are \"thin\" (empty brain dirs; conversations exist\n  only as unparsed protobuf). They are ledgered `skipped_thin`, not guessed at.\n  A `.pb` decoder or the `antigravity-backup/` dirs would raise coverage.\n- Claude coverage in the memo-ray store is 7 sessions vs 36 transcript files on\n  disk — worth a look at `claudeParser` thresholds.\n- Card quality has a 9B ceiling; every claim carries session-id citations so\n  weak cards are visible and re-runnable (`map --force` after deleting a card).\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cd3acf4-f0f5-4df1-9653-9872366abb58","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"7aba7344-6e98-4c00-b7e9-ad132cfe087b","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
