m ingestion.\n\n**How to apply:** The book path is standalone: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs reduce --only dossiers,themes,report` → `opus` → `pdf` (no ingest needed; retrieval reads existing vectors/graph). Never run deep-synthesis ingest concurrently with LLM reduce/opus phases on the same lemonade box. v1.10.1 CUT + PUSHED 2026-07-03 (~07:06 UTC): docs updated (LONGVIEW_GUIDE \"Book on demand\" + troubleshooting, scripts/longview/README 9-phase table, CLAUDE.md status), main pushed before tag, Release Desktop workflow triggered. Still open: code phase cp1252/braille UnicodeEncodeError despite PYTHONIOENCODING env (crashes benny enrich child); weave discovery-questions JSON parse failed twice that night; 32 card docs still marked un-ingested (next full run re-attempts the ~4h deep-synthesis pass).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":4,"newStart":16,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," **Why:** every coupling here was \"one slow/failing stage silently poisons or kills everything downstream\" — the user explicitly wants the book (opus) generation decoupled from ingestion."," ","+**Key stack lesson (2026-07-03 reruns):** lemonade's JSON mode (`response_format: json_object`) makes qwen3.5-9b stop mid-object at ~300 completion tokens regardless of budget, and emit stray scalars inside arrays (`\"parts\": [1, {…}]`) — while plain-text calls of the same length complete fine (dossiers 200s+, sections). It was NEVER a token-budget problem (ledger showed 280-434 completion vs 1800 budget). Fixes (commits 9344006, eaf80fb, c28fe10): trimmed outline digest + parts-first key order; `repairTruncatedJson` in llm.mjs (cut to last completed value, close containers — salvaged all 6 chapters of a real truncated outline); opus jsonCall dropped json:true entirely + validates required key holds ≥minItems objects-with-title + sanitizes disk-loaded outline + synthesizes missing section ids. Suspect the same JSON-mode flakiness behind weave discovery-question failures and ~30% map-card \"not a JSON object\" gate errors — dropping json:true there too is the likely fix if they keep failing.","+"," **How to apply:** The book path is standalone: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs reduce --only dossiers,themes,report` → `opus` → `pdf` (no ingest needed; retrieval reads existing vectors/graph). Never run deep-synthesis ingest concurrently with LLM reduce/opus phases on the same lemonade box. v1.10.1 CUT + PUSHED 2026-07-03 (~07:06 UTC): docs updated (LONGVIEW_GUIDE \"Book on demand\" + troubleshooting, scripts/longview/README 9-phase table, CLAUDE.md status), main pushed before tag, Release Desktop workflow triggered. Still open: code phase cp1252/braille UnicodeEncodeError despite PYTHONIOENCODING env (crashes benny enrich child); weave discovery-questions JSON parse failed twice that night; 32 card docs still marked un-ingested (next full run re-attempts the ~4h deep-synthesis pass)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1f947617-4a49-4645-a9a3-e6f674adddaa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"7aba7344-6e98-4c00-b7e9-ad132cfe087b","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
