d the strict `.parts.length` check → uncaught throw killed the process, taking pdf down. Related: [[project-longview-session-synthesis]].\n\nFixes (commits baa8dd1 + ac2c4e8 on main, after v1.10.0):\n\n- **kg3d synoptic web** (baa8dd1): Documents-tab \"Maximum call stack size exceeded\" = `Math.max(1, ...degree.values())` in the /graph/full fallback at ~30k concepts. Now incremental max + 400-node budget (all Sources + top-degree concepts, edges filtered). Test `settle()` had to become a macrotask drain — the fallback's second fetch outlived 5 microtasks (pre-existing red test since the fallback landed in v1.10.0).\n- **longview decoupling** (ac2c4e8): per-phase try/catch in runManifest (phase_error ledger entries, never fatal); opus jsonCall requires non-empty array for requiredKey; reduceCall retries once on empty response, never overwrites a real file with nothing, ledgers ok:false; runReduce merges case-variant project names (\"benny\"/\"Benny\" dossier files collide on Windows).\n\n**Why:** every coupling here was \"one slow/failing stage silently poisons or kills everything downstream\" — the user explicitly wants the book (opus) generation decoupled from ingestion.\n\n**Key stack lesson (2026-07-03 reruns):** lemonade's JSON mode (`response_format: json_object`) makes qwen3.5-9b stop mid-object at ~300 completion tokens regardless of budget, and emit stray scalars inside arrays (`\"parts\": [1, {…}]`) — while plain-text calls of the same length complete fine (dossiers 200s+, sections). It was NEVER a token-budget problem (ledger showed 280-434 completion vs 1800 budget). Fixes (commits 9344006, eaf80fb, c28fe10): trimmed outline digest + parts-first key order; `repairTruncatedJson` in llm.mjs (cut to last completed value, close containers — salvaged all 6 chapters of a real truncated outline); opus jsonCall dropped json:true entirely + validates required key holds ≥minItems objects-with-title + sanitizes disk-loaded outline + synthesizes missing section ids. 