ey/BlobDB). Background blob GC targets the oldest 25% of files. | Feasible — rocksdict exposes `set_enable_blob_files`, `set_min_blob_size(1024)`, `set_enable_blob_gc`, `set_blob_gc_age_cutoff(0.25)`, `set_blob_file_size(128 MB)` (probed 2026-07-03). |\n| FR2 | **Lazy LZ4 payload decompression.** Payloads are LZ4 block-compressed with a 4-byte original-size header; decompressed only on `get`. | Feasible — Python feasibility build approximates the C++ zero-copy pipeline (PinnableSlice → ONNX tensor) with buffer-level decompression; true zero-copy is a scale-phase concern (see §6). |\n| FR3 | **1-bit binary-quantized vector search.** Sign-threshold quantization (768 dims → 96 bytes), Hamming distance via hardware popcount, HNSW index (USearch, `ScalarKind.B1`). | Feasible — usearch 2.25.3 B1/Hamming probed working; numpy ≥2.0 `bitwise_count` for the exact reference backend. |\n| FR4 | **Full-precision rescore.** Binary search retrieves `k × oversample` candidates; stored float32 vectors rescore by cosine to final top-k. (Industry-standard BQ practice the original research omitted; turns 90–95% recall into ≳99%.) | Feasible — float vectors ride the same KV store. |\n| FR5 | **Chroma-compatible collection surface + feature toggle.** `S16Collection` mirrors the chromadb Collection subset Prime-Silo's RAG layer uses (`add`, `query`, `get`, `count`), and a toggle resolver lets Prime-Silo opt in via one env var — without S16 importing anything from Prime-Silo. | Feasible — see ADR-003. |\n\n## 3. Non-functional requirements\n\n| ID   | Requirement | Enforcement |\n| ---- | ----------- | ----------- |\n| NFR1 | **Determinism.** Single-threaded index construction; identical search results across rebuilds from identical input; an exact brute-force backend as the deterministic reference. | Tests assert cross-rebuild + reopen result equality; brute-force index files are bit-identical. |\n| NFR2 | **Test coverage ≥ 80% from the start.** | `pytest --cov-fail-under=80` wired into `pyproject.toml`; CI fails below the bar. |\n| NFR3 | **Sovereignty.** No network, no external service, all state under a single directory; dependencies statically distributable (wheels). | Code review + no service/socket code in the library. |\n| NFR4 | **No Prime-Silo integration until gates pass.** S16 must prove swappability standalone (gates G0–G2 in PLAN.md) before any Prime-Silo file changes. | PLAN.md phase gates; ADR-003 documents the eventual 5-line toggle patch without applying it. |\n\n## 4. Hardware routing (recorded constraint, out of feasibility scope)\n\nThe source research contained a contradiction the ADA review upheld: NPUs (OpenVINO/QNN/CoreML)\nare static tensor engines and **cannot** execute HNSW traversal, pointer chasing, or LZ4. The\ncorrected routing is a design constraint for any future accelerated build:\n\n- **NPU:** static-shape embedding generation and sign quantization only.\n- **CPU (SIMD popcount — AVX-512 `vpopcntq` / NEON `vcnt`) or GPU:** index search, KV lookups,\n  LZ4 decompression.\n- **CPU/GPU:** autoregressive decoding (dynamic shapes).\n\nThe feasibility build is CPU-only; USearch/SimSIMD provide the SIMD kernels transparently.\n\n## 5. Scale envelope\n\nDesign target: **1M vectors × 768 dims**. At the current real workload (75k concepts) the\npacked binary index is ~7 MB and brute-force scanning is already sub-millisecond — HNSW earns\nits keep at the design target, not the current size. Both backends ship; benchmarks report both.\n\n## 6. Explicit deviations from the source research\n\n1. **Python-first feasibility** (rocksdict + usearch wheels), not a custom C++/ONNX-runtime\n   operator. Rationale: Prime-Silo's inference runs in **lemonade over HTTP**, not an in-process\n   ONNX session — there is no attention window to zero-copy into today. The stateful\n   `MeshMemoryRetrieve` C++ operator remains the documented scale path if inference ever moves\n   in-process.\n2. **Rescore added** (FR4) — required for production-grade recall; absent from the source doc.\n3. **Single-writer ownership rule** — RocksDB is single-process; the eventual owner is\n   Prime-Silo's Python runtime, with other processes proxying through it (ADR-001 §Consequences).\n4. **Corrected arithmetic** — 1536-dim float32 = 6144 bytes (doc said 6048); this build is\n   768-dim (Prime-Silo's local embedder), i.e. 3072 bytes float / 96 bytes packed.\n\n## 7. Feasibility use case (the proof)\n\nSynthetic clustered corpus: 2,000 documents, 768-dim embeddings drawn from 32 seeded clusters,\ncompressible markdown-like payloads. Gates (all enforced as tests):\n\n- **Recall@10 ≥ 0.90** vs exact float-cosine ground truth (both index backends).\n- **Payload integrity** — byte-exact roundtrip through LZ4 + RocksDB.\n- **Compression ratio > 1.2×** on the corpus payloads.\n- **Determinism** — identical search results after reopen and after a from-scratch rebuild.\n- **Coverage ≥ 80%** across the library.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_read_input_tokens":286353,"output_tokens":2795,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":452,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2795,"cache_read_input_tokens":286353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":452},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ccesa9YJFJpKcebEk1W2P","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_session","attributionMcpTool":"mark_chapter","type":"assistant","uuid":"88181810-3662-42f1-b509-4f760410bbe1","timestamp":"2026-07-03T09:17:54.914Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\s16","sessionId":"7aba7344-6e98-4c00-b7e9-ad13