{"parentUuid":"0b7c27e9-3a2a-4197-9ca1-dc2bfb8015a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_013hEYberGr5jzNpoV8nBEFs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UpWR74GnqWBne4aJh1YRwC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\s16\\docs\\ADR-001-storage-engine.md","content":"# ADR-001 — Storage engine: RocksDB (rocksdict) with BlobDB key–value separation\n\n**Status:** Accepted · 2026-07-03\n\n## Context\n\nS16 needs an embedded store for three record classes per vector key: compressed payloads\n(multi-modal blobs, documents), float32 vectors (for rescore), and JSON metadata. Requirements:\nhigh sequential ingest, point lookups by 64-bit key, no external service, Windows/macOS/Linux\nwheels, deterministic behaviour.\n\nCandidates evaluated (source research + ADA review):\n\n| Engine | Verdict | Why |\n| ------ | ------- | --- |\n| **RocksDB via rocksdict** | **Chosen** | Native BlobDB key–value separation (WiscKey) exposed in the Python binding: `set_enable_blob_files`, `set_min_blob_size`, `set_enable_blob_gc`, `set_blob_gc_age_cutoff`, `set_blob_file_size` (all probed working on cp314/win64, 2026-07-03). Low write amplification (1.23–1.41×), small RSS (~250–300 MB envelope at benchmark scale). |\n| LMDB | Rejected | Best-in-class random reads but severe write amplification (1.64–1.8×), multi-GB RSS mappings, no compression, files never shrink. |\n| BadgerDB | Rejected | Go runtime GC pauses break determinism guarantees; would force a Go sidecar process. |\n| SQLite | Rejected (for this layer) | Simplest, but no KV separation — large blobs bloat the B-tree and the WAL; fine as a debug fallback, not the design. |\n\n## Decision\n\nOne `Rdict` instance in raw mode per store directory, BlobDB enabled, with the research doc's\ntuning where the binding exposes it:\n\n```python\nopts = Options(raw_mode=True)\nopts.create_if_missing(True)\nopts.set_enable_blob_files(True)        # FR1: key–value separation\nopts.set_min_blob_size(1024)            # <1 KB stays in the SST files\nopts.set_enable_blob_gc(True)           # reclaim deleted payloads\nopts.set_blob_gc_age_cutoff(0.25)       # oldest 25% of blob files per GC pass\nopts.set_blob_file_size(128 * 2**20)    # 128 MB sequential blob files\n```\n\nRecord classes are namespaced by one-byte key prefixes in a single keyspace\n(`p:` payload, `v:` vector, `m:` metadata, `s:`/`r:` string-id maps) rather than column\nfamilies — fewer moving parts at feasibility scale, and a CF migration is mechanical later.\n\nPayload values are LZ4 block-compressed with a 4-byte little-endian original-size header\n(FR2), matching the C++ scale-path format so blob files stay forward-compatible. Vector and\nmetadata values are stored raw (float32 noise doesn't compress; metadata is small).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **Single-writer rule:** RocksDB permits one writing process. When S16 reaches Prime-Silo,\n  the Python runtime owns the store; Node/MCP callers proxy through it. This must be part of\n  the integration design (ADR-003), not an afterthought.\n- Space amplification from append-only blobs is bounded by the GC settings above; the\n  known GoG (GC-over-GC) hazard on zoned storage is out of scope until a ZNS deployment exists.\n- rocksdict pins us to its wheel matrix; the exit hatch is the `BlobStore` seam — the class is\n  ~100 lines and any KV with byte keys/values can implement it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2856,"cache_read_input_tokens":286805,"output_tokens":1343,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1343,"cache_read_input_tokens":286805,"cache_creation_input_t