isfires at ~0.8ms Chroma baseline; retrieval is invisible under embed+generation | ✅ done | parity_harness.py header + ADR-003 |\n\n**G2 finding — retrieval corpus is small.** The Chroma `knowledge` collection\nholds ingested chunks (572 for longview, 422 for default), NOT the 75,864 Neo4j\nconcepts. S16 replaces the chunk-retrieval store (hundreds–low-thousands per\nworkspace); the 75k concept graph is Neo4j/Kùzu scale (P5). At this size the\nbrute-force backend alone is adequate and latency is a non-issue.","originalFile":"# PLAN — S16 solution planner & tracker\n\n**Rule:** a task is *done* only with evidence (test, file, or committed numbers). Update the\nstatus column in the same commit as the work. Phases gate each other (ADR-003 gates table).\n\n## Phase P0 — Governance scaffold\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P0.1 | Repo + venv + native deps (rocksdict, usearch, lz4, numpy) proven importable on Windows/cp314 | ✅ done | probe output in ADR-001/ADR-002 (2026-07-03) |\n| P0.2 | PRD captured, incl. scope correction (Chroma-replacement, not Neo4j) and NPU routing correction | ✅ done | docs/PRD.md |\n| P0.3 | ADR-001 storage, ADR-002 index, ADR-003 swap seam + gates | ✅ done | docs/ADR-00{1,2,3}\\*.md |\n| P0.4 | This tracker | ✅ done | docs/PLAN.md |\n\n## Phase P1 — Feasibility library (standalone, no Prime-Silo)\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P1.1 | `s16.quantize` — sign binarize, packed Hamming, cosine | ✅ done | src/s16/quantize.py + tests/test_quantize.py |\n| P1.2 | `s16.store.BlobStore` — rocksdict/BlobDB, LZ4 + 4-byte header, prefix namespaces | ✅ done | src/s16/store.py + tests/test_store.py |\n| P1.3 | `s16.index` — USearch B1 backend + exact brute-force reference, save/load/view, threads=1 | ✅ done | src/s16/index.py + tests/test_index.py |\n| P1.4 | `s16.knowledge_store.S16KnowledgeStore` — put/get/search with oversample+rescore, manifest, reopen | ✅ done | src/s16/knowledge_store.py + tests/test_knowledge_store.py |\n| P1.5 | `s16.chroma_compat.S16Collection` + `s16.toggle` (FR5) | ✅ done | src/s16/chroma_compat.py, toggle.py + tests/test_chroma_compat.py |\n| P1.6 | Feasibility use case (G0): 2k clustered docs, recall@10 ≥ 0.90 both backends, payload integrity, compression >1.2×, reopen + rebuild determinism | ✅ done | tests/test_feasibility_usecase.py |\n| P1.7 | Coverage ≥ 80% enforced (`--cov-fail-under=80`) | ✅ done | pyproject.toml + pytest run in README |\n\n## Phase P2 — Honest benchmarks (G1)\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P2.1 | Bench harness: ingest throughput, search p50/p95 (k=10), disk footprint, compression ratio, recall — both backends, 10k docs | ✅ done | bench/bench_feasibility.py |\n| P2.2 | Numbers committed | ✅ done | bench/results.json |\n\n## Phase P3 — Parity vs Chroma on real data (G2) — NOT STARTED\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P3.1 | Exporter: dump a real Prime-Silo workspace's (ids, documents, embeddings, metadatas) to a portable file — read-only against Chroma, run from Prime-Silo side | ⬜ todo | — |\n| P3.2 | Parity harness: replay export into S16 + fresh Chroma, compare top-10 overlap (≥95%), latency, footprint → parity_results.json | ⬜ todo | — |\n| P3.3 | Tune oversample / connectivity on parity data | ⬜ todo | — |\n\n## Phase P4 — Prime-Silo feature-toggle integration (G3) — GATED, NOT STARTED\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P4.1 | Toggle patch in `get_knowledge_collection` (ADR-003 §3), default OFF | ⬜ gated on G2 | — |\n| P4.2 | One workspace full ingest+retrieval cycle with `PRIME_SILO_KNOWLEDGE_STORE=s16` | ⬜ gated | — |\n| P4.3 | Single-writer ownership enforcement (runtime owns dir; doc for Node/MCP proxying) | ⬜ gated | — |\n\n## Phase P5 — Graph layer decision — SEPARATE TRACK\n\n| ID | Task | Status | Evidence |\n| --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |\n| P5.1 | Evaluate Kùzu (embedded, Cypher) against the dual-graph workload (ontology, CORRELATES_WITH joins, enrich) — the actual Neo4j replacement question | ⬜ todo | — |\n| P5.2 | ADR-004: property-graph decision (Kùzu vs adjacency-on-RocksDB vs keep Neo4j) | ⬜ todo | — |\n\n## Risk register\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n| ---- | ---------- |\n| rocksdict / usearch wheel availability drifts on future Python versions | `BlobStore` and index interfaces are seams; brute-force backend is pure numpy |\n| HNSW recall at 768-dim binary below gate on real (non-synthetic) embeddings | Oversample dial + rescore (ADR-002); parity phase measures on real data before any flip |\n| Single-writer collision at integration time | ADR-001/ADR-003 ownership rule; G3 checklist item P4.3 |\n| Synthetic feasibility corpus flatters recall | G2 parity on a real workspace export is the binding gate, not G0 |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":14,"newStart":31,"newLines":21,"lines":[" | P2.1 | Bench harness: ingest throughput, search p50/p95 (k=10), disk footprint, compression ratio, recall — both backends, 10k docs | ✅ done | bench/bench_feasibility.py |"," | P2.2 | Numbers committed | ✅ done | bench/results.json |"," ","-## Phase P3 — Parity vs Chroma on real data (G2) — NOT STARTED","+## Phase P3 — Parity vs Chroma on real data (G2) — ✅ PASSED"," "," | ID | Task | Status | Evidence |"," | --- | ---- | ------ | -------- |","-| P3.1 | Exporter: dump a real Prime-Silo workspace's (ids, documents, embeddings, metadatas) to a portable file — read-only against Chroma, run from Prime-Silo side | ⬜ todo | — |","-| P3.2 | Parity harness: replay export into S16 + fresh Chroma, compare top-10 overlap (≥95%), latency, footprint → parity_results.json | ⬜ todo | — |","-| P3.3 | Tune oversample / connectivity on parity data | ⬜ todo | — |","+| P3.1 | Exporter: dump a real Prime-Silo workspace's (ids, documents, embeddings, metadatas) to a portable file — read-only against Chroma, replays stored