{"parentUuid":"c8a1aa20-ad73-473e-86e7-b04501b4a3f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CGwjanQDzhDJK9ihomN1iv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PTsi6eMwx6PkRpZgys39fM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\s16\\docs\\INTEGRATION.md","content":"# Testing the S16 swap inside Prime-Silo (feature-toggle workflow)\n\nThe swap is **experimental and OFF by default**. This is the workflow to try it\non one workspace without committing Prime-Silo to it — \"test before going all\nin\" (ADR-003 gate G3). It ships on the Prime-Silo branch\n`feat/s16-knowledge-store-toggle`, unmerged.\n\n## What the toggle does\n\n`benny/tools/knowledge.py :: get_knowledge_collection` gained a lazy, default-OFF\nbranch:\n\n- `PRIME_SILO_KNOWLEDGE_STORE` unset → unchanged Chroma path (S16 never imported).\n- `=s16` **and** the `s16` package importable → an `S16Collection` (RocksDB +\n  USearch) sited at `<workspace>/s16_knowledge`, with Benny's\n  `LocalEmbeddingFunction` injected so text ingest and `query_texts` embed\n  exactly as before.\n- `=s16` but `s16` not installed → falls back to Chroma (ImportError swallowed).\n\nProduction installs that neither set the env var nor ship `s16` are byte-for-byte\nunaffected: the toggle branch imports nothing and returns immediately.\n\n## Proven before integration (this repo)\n\n- **G0/G1/G2** — feasibility, benchmarks, and parity vs Chroma on two real\n  exported workspaces (top-10 overlap 0.98–1.00). See PLAN.md.\n- **Live end-to-end** (`bench/integration_e2e.py`) — the exact production path\n  (documents-only `add` + `query_texts`) through `S16Collection` with the real\n  lemonade nomic embedder injected: 3/3 semantic hits, delete-by-where and\n  reopen durable.\n\n## Try it on one workspace\n\n1. Install S16 into the runtime's Python environment (the one that runs\n   `benny_cli.py` / serves the API):\n\n   ```powershell\n   <runtime-python> -m pip install -e C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\s16\n   ```\n\n2. Turn the toggle on for that process only:\n\n   ```powershell\n   $env:PRIME_SILO_KNOWLEDGE_STORE = \"s16\"\n   ```\n\n3. Ingest into a **throwaway** workspace and query it through the normal RAG\n   paths (Bridge → Documents, or `search_knowledge_workspace`). S16 data lands\n   in `<workspace>/s16_knowledge/`; the existing `<workspace>/chromadb/` is left\n   untouched, so turning the toggle back off restores Chroma instantly.\n\n4. Compare. The `knowledge` collection is small (hundreds–low-thousands of\n   chunks); retrieval should feel identical. Re-ingesting a document replaces\n   its chunks via `delete(where={\"source\": ...})`, same as Chroma.\n\n## Roll back\n\nUnset `PRIME_SILO_KNOWLEDGE_STORE` (or restart without it). To remove entirely,\n`git checkout main` in Prime-Silo — the toggle lives only on the feature branch.\n\n## Not yet done (the \"go all in\" gate, PLAN P4)\n\n- Batched persistence: `S16Collection` persists the index on every `add`/`delete`\n  for per-request correctness. A production default needs batched/deferred\n  persist to avoid rewriting the index each ingest batch.\n- Single-writer ownership: RocksDB is one-writer-per-process. The runtime must\n  own the store; Node/MCP reach retrieval through the runtime's HTTP API (they\n  already do for RAG). This must be explicit before flipping the default.\n- Ship decision: add `s16` (+ rocksdict/usearch/lz4 wheels) to the runtime\n  bundle only when the default flips — until then it stays a dev-only install.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_read_input_tokens":334520,"output_tokens":1522,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1191,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_avai