dex + BruteForceBinaryIndex exact reference) → S16KnowledgeStore (binary search + float32 cosine rescore, manifest.json pins config) → chroma_compat.S16Collection + toggle.resolve_collection (env `PRIME_SILO_KNOWLEDGE_STORE=s16`).\n\nProven (G0+G1+G2): 50 tests, 99% coverage (80% gate enforced in pyproject); recall@10=1.0 both backends; bench/results.json: 10k docs, search p50 4–6ms, ingest 9–35k docs/s. **Key measured lesson: fixed oversample silently degrades with corpus density (recall 0.58 at 10k docs w/ 8×) — the recall knee is a candidate COUNT (~320 at that density), so search uses max(k*oversample, min_candidates=384) floor; curves in ADR-002.**\n\n**G2 PASSED (2026-07-03, commit 003336e):** parity harness (bench/export_chroma.py read-only dumps stored nomic-768 vectors; bench/parity_harness.py replays into S16 + fresh cosine Chroma, compares top-10 neighborhoods excluding self). Real workspaces: longview 572 docs overlap 0.977, default 422 docs overlap 1.00, both S16 p50 ~3–4ms. **Latency gate corrected to ABSOLUTE p50≤25ms (not 2× ratio) — ratio misfires vs Chroma's ~0.8ms baseline; 3-4ms is invisible under embed+generation.** **CRITICAL scale clarification: the Chroma `knowledge` collection holds ingested CHUNKS (hundreds–low-thousands/workspace), NOT the 75,864 Neo4j concepts. S16 replaces the chunk-retrieval store at small scale (brute-force alone is adequate; latency is a non-issue). The 75k concept graph is Neo4j/Kùzu scale = separate P5 track.** chromadb is an optional `parity` extra only; library never imports it.\n\n**Why:** user wants Neo4j+JRE weight out of the zero-install bundle eventually, but demanded governance-first: PRD/ADR/tracker from day one, ≥80% coverage from the start, feasibility before any prime-silo change.\n\n**How to apply:** Do NOT touch prime-silo until gates pass: G2 = parity harness vs Chroma on a real workspace export (≥95% top-10 overlap) — PLAN P3, not started; G3 = toggle patch in benny's get_knowledge_collection, defaul